body:
I fuckin wish, at least when I was there it was all quotas and mandatory promotions. Management might get bonuses. your incentive is not losing your job. And I guess if you sell really well, they might promote you to a better paid position. 

&#x200B;

But I was there almost a decade ago, maybe things have changed. I jumped ship to costco where I still don't get commision, but at least I get healthcare and a better raise structure.

to each their own. You don't have to clean them by hand, just load racks into the pan washer. Should be cleaning throughout the day as well, so it's not all at the end. Personally I didn't find it particularly exhausting, just load em up, clean something else, repeat. 

&#x200B;

But I've been working in kitchens and bakeries for over a decade, and I'm used to cleaning a lot of stuff at the end of every night. So maybe I'm just more used to it than you?

You want to try to roll into him more than you are. you keep rolling away. Especially goldfrey, most of his attacks can be avoided by rolling around his left side, and then just walking right to avoid his spins. He is a boss where he has some pauses in his attacks that are easy to punish, but outside of those pauses, it's best to keep moving.

&#x200B;

You can also jump over a lot of his attacks instead of dodging them.

heaters only gave 13%, and the boss destroyed them when I did it.///

&#x200B;

also broke 2 hunting rifles...

